From u99a06696c483481a at groups.google.com  Thu May  9 17:04:53 2019
From: u99a06696c483481a at groups.google.com (Edward Rigdon)
Date: Thu, 09 May 2019 17:04:53 +0000
Subject: Re: How to fix the values of mean/ intercept/ threshold in the multiple group analysis
Message-ID: <zZhiMG-zjhM.zL9V1eenAAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/zZhiMG-zjhM/m/zL9V1eenAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If your factor is f, then
f ~ c(0, -0.5)*1
would work, if f is not a dependent variable. If f is dependent, then the parameter is only f's intercept, not its mean. But you could work out the equation for the mean of the factor, apply labels to model parameters, then create a constraint using those labeled parameter values.

